# Build context exclusions for the API and web images.
#
# Both Dockerfiles build from the REPOSITORY ROOT (the pnpm workspace lockfile
# and packages/* live above apps/*), so this file governs every image build.

# --- never ship credentials ------------------------------------------------
# .env is gitignored and holds real local credentials. It must not enter a
# build context: anything copied into a layer is readable in the final image
# even if a later stage deletes it. Configuration arrives as runtime env vars.
.env
.env.*
!.env.example
*.pem
*.key
*.p12
*.pfx
.aws/
credentials

# --- host build output -----------------------------------------------------
# Excluded so the image always compiles from source. Host node_modules are
# especially wrong to copy: sharp and dicom-parser resolve platform-specific
# binaries, and a glibc/WSL2 tree does not run on Alpine's musl.
**/node_modules
**/dist
**/.next
**/out
**/build
**/*.tsbuildinfo
.pnpm-store

# --- test and tooling output ----------------------------------------------
**/coverage
**/test-results
**/playwright-report
**/.vitest

# --- not needed to build or run -------------------------------------------
.git
.github
.gitleaks.toml
.dependency-cruiser.cjs
docs
infra
scripts
test-data
BUILD_SPEC.md
README.md
SECURITY.md
eslint.config.mjs
**/*.log
**/.DS_Store
**/Thumbs.db
.idea
.vscode
